Test of the Fire Storm	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Test of the Fire Storm","wikiPath":"/Test_of_the_Fire_Storm","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Temple of Veeshan","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Telkorenar","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[],"rewards":[{"text":"Cloak of the Fire Storm","item":"Cloak of the Fire Storm","wikiPath":"/Cloak_of_the_Fire_Storm"}],"card":{"title":"Test of the Fire Storm","lines":["Minimum Level: 55","Classes: Bard, Monk, Paladin, Ranger, Rogue, Shadow Knight, Warrior","Related NPCs: Dozekar the Cursed, Krigara, Lepethida, Ymmeln"]},"links":["Temple of Veeshan","Telkorenar","Bard","Monk","Paladin","Ranger","Rogue","Shadow Knight","Warrior","Dozekar the Cursed","Krigara","Lepethida","Ymmeln","Cloak of the Fire Storm","Ruby Symbol","Flame Kissed Symbol","Poison Tear","Serrated Tear","Claws of Veeshan","Yelinak","Kromzek"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Telkorenar","text":"The strong seek me out, for one reason or another. It seems you have come here in peace. Perhaps you wish to prove yourself a mighty fighter? I respect only might, ______."},{"npc":"Telkorenar","text":"For the mighty I have four tests. The test of the tooth, the test of the flame, the test of the fire storm and the test of protection. Which test do you wish to undertake?"},{"npc":"Telkorenar","text":"Become like a fire storm and bring your wrath upon the inhabitants of the halls of testing. Return when you have the tear of poison and the serrated tear along with the a symbol kissed by flames and a ruby symbol."},{"npc":"Telkorenar","text":"You have done well, ______. You have proven that you are strong, but do you dare enter those halls again?"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T09:01:44.796Z","outOfEra":true}
Key to Jaled Dar's Lair (Zlandicar)	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Key to Jaled Dar's Lair (Zlandicar)","wikiPath":"/Key_to_Jaled_Dar's_Lair_(Zlandicar)","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Dragon Necropolis","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Zlandicar","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[],"rewards":[{"text":"Jaled Dar's Tomb Key","item":"Jaled Dar's Tomb Key","wikiPath":"/Jaled_Dar%27s_Tomb_Key"}],"card":{"title":"Key to Jaled Dar's Lair (Zlandicar)","lines":["Minimum Level: 55","Classes: All","Related Zones: None","Related NPCs: Neb","Required Faction: Apprehensive or better, Sneak works!"]},"links":["Dragon Necropolis","Zlandicar","Neb","Jaled Dar's Tomb Key","Neb's head","Zlandicar (Faction)","Claws of Veeshan","Chetari","Ring of Scale","Key to Jaled Dar's Lair (Neb)"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Zlandicar","text":"Hmm, I have been watching you. You made it further than I thought you would. I will have to work on my defenses in the future. So, what do you seek of me?"},{"npc":"Zlandicar","text":"Jaled Dar is quite dead, you know. But he was tasty, I feasted on his remains long ago. I do wish his spirit would go away, his incessant wailing disturbs me, and worse, it makes other dragons wary of this place. I have not eaten as well as I would have liked since his shade came to stay. If you wish to speak with him yourself, I can arrange that, for I hold a key that will unlock his tomb."},{"npc":"Zlandicar","text":"This IS my realm, after all. Nothing is barred to me. But I did not become who I am by doing something for nothing. If you wish to talk to Jaled Dar, you will have to do something for me first. Are you willing to do this task?"},{"npc":"Zlandicar","text":"There is an annoying uprising taking place among the Chetari and Paebala. This is affecting my diet. I get cranky when I don't eat right. I am VERY cranky right now. The rebellion is led by a Paebala named Neb. He has taken his followers into a part of the Necropolis that I have difficulty reaching, and he has somehow tamed the goo there as well, preventing my Chetari followers from assaulting them directly. If Neb were to fall, I am certain the rebellion would quickly falter. Bring me Neb's head, and I will give you the key to Jaled Dar's tomb."},{"npc":"Zlandicar","text":"Excellent work! Here is your key, go bother that prattling fool Jaled Dar, and leave me be."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T09:01:45.898Z","outOfEra":true}
Monk Headband Quests#Blue and Black Headband	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Monk Headband Quests","wikiPath":"/Monk_Headband_Quests","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"North Qeynos","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Phin Esrinap, Togahn Sorast","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[],"rewards":[{"text":"White Headband","item":"White Headband","wikiPath":"/White_Headband"},{"text":"Yellow Headband","item":"Yellow Headband","wikiPath":"/Yellow_Headband"},{"text":"Orange Headband","item":"Orange Headband","wikiPath":"/Orange_Headband"},{"text":"Red Headband","item":"Red Headband","wikiPath":"/Red_Headband"},{"text":"Purple Headband","item":"Purple Headband","wikiPath":"/Purple_Headband"}],"card":{"title":"Monk Headband Quests","lines":["Minimum Level: 1-30 (progresses)","Classes: Monk","Related Zones: Various","Related NPCs: Various"]},"links":["Qeynos","Phin Esrinap","Togahn Sorast","Monk","Silent Fist Clan","White Headband","Yellow Headband","Orange Headband","Red Headband","Purple Headband","Gnoll Pup Scalp","Guards of Qeynos","Ashen Order","Putrid Rib Bone","A putrid skeleton","Qeynos Hills","Blackburrow","Surefall Glade","A dread corpse","Blackburrow Gnoll Pelt","Blackburrow Gnoll Skin","Dareb's Skull","High Shaman Phido","Head of Shen","High Shaman Grisok","Head of Ghanex Drah","Ghanex Drah","Skull of Jhen`Tra","A gnoll embalmer","Lake Rathetear","Dagger of Marnek","The thaumaturgist","Befallen","Zaharn's Coronet","High Priest Zaharn","Permafrost","Robe of the Lost Circle","Note for Konem","Monk Sash Quests","Monks of The Whistling Fist"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"Hello, my name is Phin. Practice, practice, practice.. That's my motto. It is my responsibility to train our members, and help them to advance their skills and abilities. I also reward our members with colored [Headbands] for completing certain tasks."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"Yes, I give the [White, Yellow, and Orange Headbands] to our newer members, and Togahn gives out [Red, Purple, and Blue Headbands] to our elder members."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"That is our training headband.. Beginning students can earn this by slaying four [gnoll] pups, and bringing their scalps back to me."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"Good.. the more of these vile dogs we slay, the safer the citizens of Qeynos will be."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"Good.. the more of these vile dogs we slay, the safer the citizens of Qeynos will be."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"Good.. the more of these vile dogs we slay, the safer the citizens of Qeynos will be."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"Good job, Soandso, keep up the good work! Here is your white training headband. Wear it with honor, and make Lu'Sun proud."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"This is awarded to our students for helping clear out the evil that inhabits the old ruins of the Qeynos Hills. Just bring me back three putrid rib bones as proof of your good deeds and turn in your [training headband], and then I will give you the yellow headband."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"Ahh.. Good. I feel that your hard work and training will soon be rewarded.. and the yellow headband shall soon be yours."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"Ahh.. Good. I feel that your hard work and training will soon be rewarded.. and the yellow headband shall soon be yours."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"Ahh.. Good. I feel that your hard work and training will soon be rewarded.. and the yellow headband shall soon be yours."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"This is a difficult award to obtain. The city of Qeynos is, as you know, under constant attack by the gnolls of Blackburrow. The Silent Fist Clan rewards its members who venture deep into this gnoll stronghold and bring swift justice to these vile creatures. Please return two Blackburrow gnoll pelts - make sure they aren't ruined - and a Blackburrow gnoll skin as proof of your noble actions. Also, turn in your [yellow headband], and then I shall give you the orange one. Good luck."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"Good work, Soandso. You are well on your way toward earning the orange headband."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"Good work, Soandso. You are well on your way toward earning the orange headband."},{"npc":"Phin Esrinap","text":"Good work, Soandso. You are well on your way toward earning the orange headband."},{"npc":"Togahn Sorast","text":"Greetings.. I am Second Master Togahn Sorast. I am here to teach the ways of our guild. For our more advanced members, I will give out [headbands] as a reward for their contribution to the clan."},{"npc":"Togahn Sorast","text":"The Silent Fist Clan gives out colored Headbands for various deeds completed by our students. [Phin] gives out the [White, Yellow, and Orange Headbands].. and I give out the [Red, Purple, and Blue Headbands]."},{"npc":"Togahn Sorast","text":"Ah, you think you are skilled enough to earn the red headband of the Silent Fist Clan, Soandso ? Hmmm.. Well, if you can help us find [Brother Dareb], you would certainly deserve the honor of wearing the red headband."},{"npc":"Togahn Sorast","text":"Yes, brother Dareb was last heard from over two weeks ago. He was out in the Plains of South Karana, and then just disappeared. We fear that those vile gnolls fleeing Splitpaw may have captured him or worse. We sent brother Shen to go search the Karanas and look for Dareb over three days ago, but haven't heard from him, either. I fear the worst for both of them, especially if the [Splitpaws] are involved. Please, Soandso , find and return our lost brothers to us. If they are not alive, bring back their remains so we may give them a proper burial.. and, if it is that evil [Ghanex Drah]'s doing, bring me his head as well, for the honor of the clan. You do this for us, Soandso , and turn in your orange headband, and I will reward you with the red headband of the Silent Fist. Good luck."},{"npc":"Togahn Sorast","text":"The Splitpaws were a large clan of gnolls that lived in a burrow out in South Karana, They have recently been ousted from their home by a new clan of gnolls that are very powerful. We try to stay away from them if we can, for we do not know much about this new breed. The Splitpaws are on the move and now is the only time to strike. If we wait too long, there will be no way to find our brother. Go now my friend, we haven't much time."},{"npc":"Togahn Sorast","text":"Ghanex Drah is ruler of the now fleeing gnolls of Splitpaw. I've heard rumors that he has been dabbling in the dark art of necromancy. Ghanex is looking for more test subjects, no doubt to rebuild his stronghold. The good people of Antonica must put an end to his evil reign soon, or I fear he could grow much more powerful."},{"npc":"Togahn Sorast","text":"We are deeply honored to have such great warrior as part of our Clan. With a proper burial, Shen and Dareb's souls will finally be at peace, and with the death of that vile Ghanex, the plains will be much safer for travelers. It is a great honor to present you, Soandso, with the red headband of the Silent Fist Clan."},{"npc":"Togahn Sorast","text":"Ah, you think you are now skilled enough to deserve the purple headband of the Silent Fist Clan? Very well, Soandso, I have a task for you that will prove whether or not you are worthy of this honor. I have heard recent rumors of ancient evils surfacing once again throughout Antonica. These evil groups have discovered some items that are giving them mystical and dangerous powers. These items must be destroyed, or else the evils of Norrath may gain control of the world's future. Bring me these [evil items], and turn in your red headband, and you will have proven yourself a mighty spirit and dedicated member of the Silent Fist."},{"npc":"Togahn Sorast","text":"These evil creations have been found all over Antonica, and no one knows, or at least no one admits to knowing, where exactly they were found, but we do know that they are currently in the wrong hands and must be destroyed. Please, Soandso, seek out the [Skull of Jhen'Tra], the [Dagger of Marnek], and the [Coronet of Buried Blood], and bring them to me."},{"npc":"Togahn Sorast","text":"I don't know much about the Skull of Jhen'Tra. I've heard that it has resurfaced in the gnoll burial grounds of Lake Rathetear. Apparently, this skull is helping to give these gnolls the power to raise an undead army of their fallen ancestors. This evil must be stopped before their army becomes too powerful."},{"npc":"Togahn Sorast","text":"The Dagger of Marnek is a diabolical weapon created by the ancient necromancer Marnek Jaull. Marnek was the leader of a small cult of necromancers who worshipped Solusek Ro. Marnek used this dagger in his ceremonial sacrifices to the Burning Prince, to increase his own power and show his loyalty to his god. His cult grew stronger and word of the evil acts spread all over Antonica. Legend has it that a group of paladins from Erudin, followers of Prexus, spent over 10 years searching out Marnek and his followers, and finally destroyed them. Though Marnek's evil reign was put to an end, many of his books and items are still being uncovered to this day. The Dagger of Marnek is now being used by the evil inhabitants who control the depths of Befallen. Bring this dagger to me, so that we may dispose of it and banish its evil powers forever."},{"npc":"Togahn Sorast","text":"The Coronet of Buried Blood is an ancient headdress which is said to have belonged to the High Priest of the Plexant Temple. The Plexant were known to be devout followers of Innoruuk and the coronet is supposed to have been blessed by the Prince of Hate himself. Apparently, the coronet is now in the hands of a clan of goblins that dwell in the caverns of Permafrost."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T09:47:50.983Z","outOfEra":false}
